This repository is a release snapshot of a Lean 4 formalization of the qutrit, three-copy part of
Theorem 2.1 and Corollary 2.2 of the PSI manuscript "Three-copy nondistillability of qutrit and
ququart Werner states" (version of 21 October 2026). The Lean files ThreeCopyQutritWerner.lean,
Solution.lean and those under
ThreeCopyQutritWerner/ (except Audit/FinalCheck.lean), and the certificate data under
verification/matrix-literals/ and verification/finite-integer-literals/, are taken from PSI's
development repository. The data files are unchanged. The Lean files are changed only as follows:
- Module system: every file starts with `module`, its imports are `public import`, and its body is
  in an `@[expose] public section` (definition bodies visible to importing modules) or, in the 12
  files that hold the metaprograms (the elaborators that read the data files and the commands that
  generate data definitions), in a `public meta section`; in those 12 files, 20 imports are
  repeated as `public meta import`. Mathlib imports are added so that each file
  sees the same Mathlib modules as before.
- In ThreeCopyQutritWerner/CertificateX2PackedLiteral.lean, the helper that adds each generated data
  definition calls `addDecl (forceExpose := true)` instead of `addDecl`, so that importing modules
  see the values of these definitions; the definitions are still checked by Lean's kernel.
- In ThreeCopyQutritWerner/CertificateLocalFramesData.lean, the line
  `set_option maxHeartbeats 400000 in` is added before each of the definitions
  certificateLocalFrameEntries0_6, certificateLocalFrameEntries1_6 and
  certificateLocalFrameEntries2_6 (a larger elaboration time budget; the definitions are unchanged).
- Solution.lean gets one new theorem, minimum_formula_unequal_dims (Theorem 2.1, unequal local
  dimensions, the case 2 <= d_i <= 3), which applies minimum_formula_of_card_of_endpoint to
  qutritEndpointInequality.
- Comments and docstrings are edited, among them those that named the manuscript's title or its
  ququart seed (in Basic.lean, NoisyFamily.lean and NoisyFamilyReduction.lean);
  ThreeCopyQutritWerner.lean and Solution.lean get new docstrings.
The files Challenge.lean and ThreeCopyQutritWerner/Audit/FinalCheck.lean are written for this
release.

The checks that passed on this commit are recorded in verification/RECEIPTS.md.

